{title: Brighten the Corner Where You Are}
{artist: Ina Ogdon & Charles Gabriel}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[F]Do not wait until some deed of [Bb]greatness you may [F]do,
do not wait to shed your light a[G]far — [C]
to the [F]many duties ever [Bb]near you now be [F]true:
brighten the [C]corner where you [F]are.

Chorus
[F]Brighten the corner where you [Bb]are, [F]brighten the corner where you [C]are;
some[F]one far from harbor you may [Bb]guide across the [F]bar —
brighten the [C]corner where you [F]are.
